	(text_box "MCU_PWR_LATCH is a control signal from the MCU that turns on the small NPN transistor, which keeps the main PMOS switched on so power continues flowing to the regulator after you let go of the button; when the MCU drives this signal low, the transistor releases the PMOS gate and the whole system turns off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
